## Workflow

- Fork the repository and create a branch from `main`.
- Keep changes small and covered: the suite is the contract.
- Run the full suite before pushing:

```console
$ python3 -m pytest -q tests
```

## Code layout

| module | what it owns |
|---|---|
| `quaydoc/lexer.py`, `quaydoc/parser.py` | source text to document tree |
| `quaydoc/inline.py` | inline markup |
| `quaydoc/slugs.py` | canonical anchors (the single source of truth) |
| `quaydoc/links.py` | reference resolution and fragment targets |
| `quaydoc/toc.py` | heading ids and the table of contents |
| `quaydoc/blocks.py`, `quaydoc/html.py` | rendering |
| `quaydoc/check.py` | the integrity checker |
| `quaydoc/cli.py` | the command line |

## Invariants

The most important invariant in the codebase is that heading ids and link
fragments are computed by two different modules that must produce identical
output. When a change touches either side, the other side must change with
it — the checker is the guard that catches drift. The release-notes history
(see the CHANGELOG) documents one incident where this invariant was broken
and every fragment link on affected pages stopped working.
